---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiLandingHero from '../components/AiLandingHero.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../data/contact';

const context = 'AI-assisted implementation';
---

<Base
  title="Implement and adapt a public service | Registry Stack"
  description="Adapt open-source registry software to your forms, rules and systems. Our team uses AI to configure and test one government service with you in a pilot."
  ogImagePath="/og-ai.png"
  ogImageAlt="Registry Stack: Design, adapt and access public services with AI."
>
  <SiteHeader current="customization" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <AiLandingHero
      eyebrow="AI-assisted implementation"
      heading="Build a service around your rules."
      lead="Adapt open-source registry software to your forms, rules and review steps. Our team uses AI to draft the configuration and test cases. Your institution reviews, tests and approves each change."
      context={context}
      exampleHref="#change-example"
      exampleLabel="See a change example"
      note="Available through a scoped implementation pilot."
    >
      <p class="ai-example-label">Example: proposed change</p>
      <p class="ai-example-title">Open enrolment to five-year-olds</p>
      <dl class="ai-example-rows">
        <div><dt>Entry age</dt><dd>6 years to <strong>5 years</strong></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Turns five by the cut-off</dt><dd>Meets the age rule</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Turns five after the cut-off</dt><dd>Does not meet the age rule</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="ai-example-status">Drafted with AI. Tests pass. Waiting for your approval.</p>
    </AiLandingHero>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="change-example" aria-labelledby="change-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Example: school enrolment</p>
          <h2 id="change-title">Change one rule across the whole service</h2>
          <p>An education authority lowers the entry age for pre-primary school. That affects what the service checks, what staff tell parents and what appears in the assignment notice.</p>
          <p>Our team uses AI to draft the changes. The education authority reviews the proposed behavior and the test results, then approves the release.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-callout">
          <h3>What the team checks before release</h3>
          <dl class="change-checks">
            <div><dt>Eligibility</dt><dd>The service applies the cut-off date for the correct school year.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>An approved age check uses the revised rule and has an agreed fallback.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Notice</dt><dd>The assignment letter names the right programme and start date.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Guidance</dt><dd>The portal and school office give parents the same information.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="change-checks" aria-labelledby="checks-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="checks-title">Each change is tested before release</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Your rules are files your team keeps</h3>
            <p>The service reads its configuration from files kept in version control. Before release, a comparison lists each change from the version in use and marks the changes that need review.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Test cases for allowed and refused requests</h3>
            <p>Each service keeps test cases: requests that must be allowed and requests that must be refused. They run again on every change.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>A failed check stops the release</h3>
            <p>The service refuses to start with a configuration that fails its checks. Your team approves the change after the checks pass.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">For technical teams: <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/operate/breg/#check-test-package">read how a configuration is checked, tested and packaged</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="how-customization-works" aria-labelledby="pilot-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="pilot-title">What you agree in an implementation pilot</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Fit with your existing systems</h3>
            <p>We assess where reusable records, forms or review steps can help. Together we agree what to configure, which systems to connect and where the service will run.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Cases to try before going live</h3>
            <p>Try a typical request and an exception. Check what people can see, who records the decision and who can make the resulting change.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>What your team will take over</h3>
            <p>Agree which configuration, tests and operating instructions your team receives, and who will run the service and maintain each connection. The service your team takes over runs on its configured rules, with no AI model required.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">Still defining the service? <a href="/ai/service-design/">See how to prepare a service brief</a>. You can also <a href="https://marketplace.registrystack.org/">browse starting configurations</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="delivery-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">AI in delivery</p>
          <h2 id="delivery-title">How we use AI in your pilot</h2>
          <p>Our team works from your forms, rules and fictional example cases. Agree the AI tools and data your institution allows before the pilot starts. Your team reviews the proposed changes and test results before approving a release.</p>
        </div>
        <section id="studio" class="editorial-callout" aria-labelledby="studio-title">
          <p class="eyebrow">In development</p>
          <h3 id="studio-title">Registry Studio</h3>
          <p>An authoring workspace for reviewing records, service steps and proposed changes.</p>
          <a class="inline-cta" href="/products/studio/">Explore Registry Studio <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 id="next-title">Scope one implementation pilot</h2>
        <p>Bring a public form and a fictional example of what you need to change. We’ll discuss what to build and test. Tell us which AI tools and data your institution allows, and we will work within them.</p>
        <div class="section-links">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">View implementation options</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .change-checks { margin: 0; }
  .change-checks > div { border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule); padding: 10px 0; }
  .change-checks > div:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .change-checks dt { color: var(--registry-ink); font-weight: 700; }
  .change-checks dd { line-height: 1.5; margin: 2px 0 0; }
  #studio { scroll-margin-top: 78px; }
</style>
